From b311526385d14bb2c1f09dc3c885df84187aa79d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98ystein=20Lie?= <oeystein@gengartv.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:50:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] media: gc550: add ALSA PCM capture integration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add ALSA PCM capture subdriver for the AVerMedia Live Gamer Extreme
(GC550).

Audio samples arrive multiplexed in the SuperSpeed bulk transport
stream (Endpoint 0x83) immediately following each video frame's EAV
marker, prefixed by marker 00 FF FF 58 and a 32-bit big-endian length
field. The stream carries uncompressed LPCM 16-bit LE stereo at 48 kHz.

Key functionality:
- Standard ALSA PCM capture device registering as "hw:GC550Audio,0".
- gc550_audio_push_samples extracting PCM packets and updating ring.
- Safe ring pointer synchronization using alsa_lock.
- Atomic waitqueue quiesce mechanism (gc550_audio_quiesce) ensuring
  safe teardown without race conditions during close or disconnect.

Signed-off-by: Øystein Lie <oeystein@gengartv.com>
---
